BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A. Rimbaud
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T211500
DTSTAMP:20261021T010000Z
UID:a-rimbaud-2026-10-20-18:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:The improbable life of French poet Arthur Rimbaud unfolds with
  all the shock and playfulness of his poetry.\n\nPatrick Wang\, United Sta
 tes & Canada\, 2026\, 175 min\, in English and French with English subtitl
 es\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/a-rimbaud/\n\nEstimated start: 18:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Autumn Afternoon (1962)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T224500
DTSTAMP:20261010T033000Z
UID:an-autumn-afternoon-2026-10-09-20:30:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:The last film by Yasujiro Ozu was also his final masterpiece\,
  a gently heartbreaking story about a man’s dignified resignation to lif
 e’s shifting currents and society’s modernization. Though the widower 
 Shuhei (frequent Ozu leading man Chishu Ryu) has been living comfortably f
 or years with his grown daughter\, a series of events leads him to accept 
 and encourage her marriage and departure from their home. As elegantly com
 posed and achingly tender as any of the Japanese master’s films\, An Aut
 umn Afternoon is one of cinema’s fondest farewells.\n\nYasujirō Ozu\, 1
 962\, Japan\, 113 min\, in Japanese with English subtitles\n\nhttps://nwfi
 lmforum.org/films/an-autumn-afternoon/\n\nEstimated start: 20:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
