BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SFCS at 10: Green Room (2016)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T205500
DTSTAMP:20261015T020000Z
UID:sfcs-10-green-room-2026-10-14-19:00:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:Special Introduction by Matt Oakes of Silver Screen Riot\n\nGr
 een Room is a brilliantly crafted and wickedly fun horror-thriller starrin
 g Patrick Stewart as a diabolical club owner who squares off against an un
 suspecting but resilient young punk band.\n\nDown on their luck punk rocke
 rs The Ain’t Rights are finishing up a long and unsuccessful tour\, and 
 are about to call it quits when they get an unexpected booking at an isola
 ted\, run-down club deep in the backwoods of Oregon. What seems merely to 
 be a third-rate gig escalates into something much more sinister when they 
 witness an act of violence backstage that they weren’t meant to see. Now
  trapped backstage\, they must face off against the club’s depraved owne
 r\, Darcy Banker (Stewart)\, a man who will do anything to protect the sec
 rets of his nefarious enterprise. But while Darcy and his henchmen think t
 he band will be easy to get rid of\, The Ain’t Rights prove themselves m
 uch more cunning and capable than anyone expected\, turning the tables on 
 their unsuspecting captors and setting the stage for the ultimate life-or-
 death showdown.\n\nJeremy Saulnier\, 2016\, United States\, 95 min\, in En
 glish\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/sfcs-10-green-room/\n\nEstimated st
 art: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SFCS at 10: Moonlight (2016)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261209T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261209T211500
DTSTAMP:20261210T030000Z
UID:sfcs-10-moonlight-2026-12-09-19:00:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:Special introduction by Timothy Hall of The People’s Critic
 \n\nA timeless story of human connection and self-discovery\, Moonlight ch
 ronicles the life of a young black man from childhood to adulthood as he s
 truggles to find his place in the world while growing up in a rough neighb
 orhood of Miami. At once a vital portrait of contemporary African-American
  life and an intensely personal and poetic meditation on identity\, family
 \, friendship\, and love\, Moonlight is a groundbreaking piece of cinema t
 hat reverberates with deep compassion and universal truths. Anchored by ex
 traordinary performances from a tremendous ensemble cast\, Barry Jenkins
 ’s staggering\, singular vision is profoundly moving in its portrayal of
  the moments\, people\, and unknowable forces that shape our lives and mak
 e us who we are.\n\nBarry Jenkins\, 2016\, United States\, 111 min\, in En
 glish\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/sfcs-10-moonlight/\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SFCS at 10: The Witch (2016)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T202500
DTSTAMP:20261120T023000Z
UID:sfcs-10-witch-2026-11-19-18:30:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:Special introduction by Bob Foster of Cinema Crazed\n\nNew Eng
 land\, 1630. Upon threat of banishment by the church\, an English farmer l
 eaves his colonial plantation\, relocating his wife and five children to a
  remote plot of land on the edge of an ominous forest—within which lurks
  an unknown evil. Strange and unsettling things begin to happen almost imm
 ediately—animals turn malevolent\, crops fail\, and one child disappears
  as another becomes seemingly possessed by an evil spirit. With suspicion 
 and paranoia mounting\, family members accuse teenage daughter Thomasin of
  witchcraft\, charges she adamantly denies. As circumstances grow more tre
 acherous\, each family member’s faith\, loyalty and love become tested i
 n shocking and unforgettable ways.\n\nIn this exquisitely made and terrify
 ing new horror film\, the age-old concepts of witchcraft\, black magic and
  possession are innovatively brought together to tell the intimate and riv
 eting story of one family’s frightful unraveling in the New England wild
 erness.\n\nRobert Eggers\, 2016\, United States\, 92 min\, in English\n\nh
 ttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/sfcs-10-witch/\n\nEstimated start: 18:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Screamplay (1984)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T182500
DTSTAMP:20261010T233000Z
UID:screamplay-4k-restoration-2026-10-10-16:30:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:“…takes HOLLYWOOD by the throat and STRANGLES it!”\n\nEd
 gar Allan (Rufus B. Seder) is an aspiring screenwriter who has just come t
 o Hollywood to make it in the movies… only to wind up working as the jan
 itor at a fleabag apartment complex run by the greasy ex-boxer Martin (Geo
 rge Kuchar) instead. When Edgar begins channeling his frustrations with hi
 s kooky neighbors into fodder for his latest screenplay\, the vivid murder
  scenes he writes begin to happen for real. As the bodies begin to pile up
  and the line between reality and fiction become increasingly blurred\, Ed
 gar\, who is convinced that the only way to be a real writer is to suffer
 \, is slowly driven mad.\n\nInventively produced using a host of early cin
 ematic techniques and featuring a memorable performance by underground fil
 m legend George Kuchar\, Rufus Butler Seder’s Screamplay is a singularly
  charming tribute to Old Hollywood and a marvel of low-budget but high-con
 cept filmmaking. New 4K restoration by Muscle Distribution in association 
 with Matchbox Cine.\n\nRufus Butler Seder\, United States\, 1984\, 93 min
 \, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/screamplay-4k-restoration/
 \n\nEstimated start: 16:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
